FTP
in active ftp, machine 1 can contact a server and ask for a control channel to be established on FTP port 21, and a data channel on port 20. 
in passive ftp, the machine may be blocked by the firewall from establishing the data channel, so the server must instead respond with the port for the control channel, thus bypassing the restriction (should port 21 be free to use the network)

TFTP
(trivial FTP)
does not provide user authentication, but uses UDP instead, so if a fragment of data is missed, the download will be corrupted
only ever used on protected interior networks

vsFTPd
